# Elixir — pip-audit waiver list (V0.16, Phase 3 / task 3.5)
# ============================================================
# One vulnerability ID per line (OSV or GHSA alias, as printed by
# pip-audit). Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored; inline
# trailing comments (# ...) are stripped.
#
# EVERY waiver must carry: (a) the affected package + pinned version,
# (b) why the finding is not exploitable in Elixir's threat model, and
# (c) a review date. The CI audit job prints a ::notice per active
# waiver so waived findings stay visible in every run.
#
# The gate: pip-audit runs over requirements.lock --no-deps with all
# --ignore-vuln args built from this file; any NON-waived known
# vulnerability fails the job. This is deliberately stricter than
# "high-severity only" — pip-audit does not expose severity ratings,
# and a stricter gate can only be safer.
#
# Currently active waivers: NONE (baseline run: 0 known vulnerabilities
# in the 105-pin core closure).
